      "content": "I'll start by reading both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `apr1Crypt` with an all-zero 8-byte password and a `null` salt produces a deterministic APR1 hash (the EvoSuite mock environment makes `SecureRandom` deterministic, yielding the salt `\"........\"`).\n\nLet me write the improved version with better naming, a descriptive test name, and a clarifying comment.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test uses a descriptive method name (`test_apr1Crypt_withNullSalt_generatesSaltAndReturnsExpectedHash`), a named variable for the expected hash, a renamed password variable (`allZeroPassword`), and a Javadoc comment explaining why the result is deterministic despite the null salt."
